1
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,660
=Bionic Trace=

2
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,620
=Episode 14=

3
00:01:24,190 --> 00:01:25,310
What a shame.

4
00:01:26,590 --> 00:01:28,190
Once again, I'm not the

5
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:29,400
perfect woman you designed.

6
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:35,550
Noi.

7
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,950
You were sacrificed

8
00:01:37,950 --> 00:01:39,120
in my pursuit of perfection.

9
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:41,160
You've suffered so much.

10
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:42,310
I'm sorry.

11
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:48,270
I know you want to kill me.

12
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:51,590
Go ahead.

13
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:54,400
This moment of mercy means nothing.

14
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:56,870
I really will kill you.

15
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,230
I respect your choice.

16
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,190
Don't move!

17
00:02:15,190 --> 00:02:15,600
Don't move!

18
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,470
Drop your weapon!

19
00:02:17,190 --> 00:02:18,000
No!

20
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:18,800
Don't shoot!

21
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:19,880
It's all my fault.

22
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,000
No!

23
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,440
Noi!

24
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,360
Noi!

25
00:03:18,390 --> 00:03:20,110
Song Yang, where have you gone?

26
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:22,190
Attention, everyone.

27
00:03:23,190 --> 00:03:24,600
Search every corner of this place.

28
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,320
Find him at all costs.

29
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,320
Captain Deng.

30
00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:29,390
The system has detected

31
00:03:29,390 --> 00:03:30,670
traces of Song Yang and Ada.

32
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,520
Move immediately.

33
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,160
Let's go.

34
00:03:35,390 --> 00:03:36,470
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

35
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:09,600
Song Yang.

36
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:11,550
I think you're still

37
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:12,880
using your own hands

38
00:04:13,390 --> 00:04:14,910
to build a better future.

39
00:04:15,270 --> 00:04:16,350
You don't need to comfort me.

40
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:17,880
I know what I'm doing.

41
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:19,920
In that case,

42
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,390
I have a question for you.

43
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:23,440
Go ahead.

44
00:04:25,270 --> 00:04:26,230
When we left

45
00:04:26,230 --> 00:04:27,480
the conference hall,

46
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:28,920
you said you hadn't come

47
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,200
just for the mission.

48
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,720
I've replaced the joint control unit

49
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:46,550
in your right arm.

50
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,640
I've also repaired most
of the other damage.

51
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,550
You should be able to move normally now.

52
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:51,950
By the way,

53
00:04:52,230 --> 00:04:53,390
what were you saying?

54
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:55,440
Nothing.

55
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:02,250
Based on an initial assessment,

56
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,320
my mobility is 12%

57
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,750
below its original level.

58
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:08,600
You're supposed to thank me.

59
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:20,270
Thank you, Song Yang.

60
00:05:25,550 --> 00:05:26,320
Something's wrong.

61
00:05:27,830 --> 00:05:28,760
I've installed several types

62
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:30,350
of surveillance equipment
in this building.

63
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:33,440
Everything seems normal so far.

64
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:37,270
But the biological detectors

65
00:05:37,270 --> 00:05:38,600
along the surrounding roads

66
00:05:39,110 --> 00:05:40,172
(Liu Wenwen, Song Yang's lover)
suddenly show readings

67
00:05:40,172 --> 00:05:41,260
(deceased, key associated person)
several times higher than normal.

68
00:06:02,390 --> 00:06:03,240
We need to leave.

69
00:06:05,310 --> 00:06:06,800
What about your equipment?

70
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:09,670
I've entered a command.

71
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,040
In three minutes,

72
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:12,880
the main computer
and hard drives will explode.

73
00:06:21,530 --> 00:06:22,110
Let's go.

74
00:06:55,510 --> 00:06:56,040
Be careful.

75
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:56,950
They've probably set up surveillance

76
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:58,320
all around us.

77
00:06:58,720 --> 00:06:59,440
I doubt my interference

78
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,640
will help much.

79
00:07:00,950 --> 00:07:01,830
What should we do?

80
00:07:04,830 --> 00:07:06,200
That's why I've prepared Plan B.

81
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:23,180
(LICENSED TO CARRY)

82
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:26,020
(Human body temperature analysis,
heat signatures: Uniform, normal)

83
00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:37,160
Have a seat.

84
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,760
It's a little cramped.

85
00:07:45,070 --> 00:07:46,380
We'll have to make do for now.

86
00:07:48,390 --> 00:07:50,070
If it weren't for me...

87
00:07:50,230 --> 00:07:52,640
This was part of the plan
from the beginning.

88
00:07:53,350 --> 00:07:54,790
It just happened a little earlier.

89
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,070
You're an android.

90
00:07:57,070 --> 00:07:58,790
Why are you even more
sentimental than humans?

91
00:08:01,510 --> 00:08:03,600
As Professor Shen Yu would put it,

92
00:08:05,110 --> 00:08:06,830
this is female empathy.

93
00:08:08,670 --> 00:08:11,440
Do androids have a sense of gender, too?

94
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,600
We're assigned a gender at the factory.

95
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,070
But it's also our choice.

96
00:08:17,510 --> 00:08:19,790
The feminine qualities
Professor Shen Yu described

97
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,390
are what I hope to develop.

98
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:32,470
What you're hoping to develop

99
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:35,230
might be a little inconvenient.

100
00:08:36,230 --> 00:08:38,200
I think it's quite convenient.

101
00:08:42,030 --> 00:08:43,230
So you're

102
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,910
planning to face off

103
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:46,880
against that so-called

104
00:08:46,910 --> 00:08:48,000
perfect woman?

105
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,880
Actually, I'm just like Noi.

106
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:55,470
We both just want to be ourselves.

107
00:08:58,230 --> 00:08:59,230
That's good.

108
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,470
Being yourself.

109
00:09:01,710 --> 00:09:04,110
Anyway, this is our new safe house.

110
00:09:05,710 --> 00:09:07,520
Ms. Shen has also given me

111
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:08,440
a new direction for the investigation.

112
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,110
You don't need to worry too much.

113
00:09:12,790 --> 00:09:13,550
Okay.

114
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:54,060
(Liu Ying and Liu Wenwen,
mother and daughter)

115
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,200
Song Yang.

116
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:57,710
What kind of truth

117
00:09:57,710 --> 00:09:58,960
are you trying to uncover?

118
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:21,980
(Zhang Mingxuan, book sales report)

119
00:10:52,110 --> 00:10:53,350
I've tried several
different medications.

120
00:10:53,350 --> 00:10:54,760
Why isn't anything working?

121
00:11:12,110 --> 00:11:12,910
Ada.

122
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,200
I discovered that two months ago,

123
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:16,030
there was a theft at Cedar.

124
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:18,350
But neither the media nor the police

125
00:11:18,350 --> 00:11:19,400
reported it.

126
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:20,440
(Universal Index System)
After that,

127
00:11:20,590 --> 00:11:22,520
three major murder cases occurred.

128
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:24,030
I wonder if those cases

129
00:11:24,030 --> 00:11:25,230
could be connected.

130
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:27,640
Ada.

131
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:36,350
Ada.

132
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:38,350
Ada.

133
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:42,290
Sorry, Song Yang.

134
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:44,700
I was just reading novels online.

135
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,320
The more androids learn

136
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:47,640
about human art and literature,

137
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:49,640
the better they can assist humans.

138
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:50,550
So what have you been reading?

139
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:52,910
So far, I've read twelve

140
00:11:52,910 --> 00:11:55,200
literary novels exploring
the existence of androids,

141
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:57,280
257 romance novels...

142
00:11:57,470 --> 00:11:58,840
Why are you reading romance novels?

143
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,400
And 1,971

144
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,470
mystery novels.

145
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:04,000
Plus 9,857 horror novels.

146
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:04,520
Stop.

147
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:06,350
Why are you reading horror novels?

148
00:12:06,590 --> 00:12:08,350
Does that help you serve humans?

149
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,550
Horror novels can stimulate

150
00:12:09,550 --> 00:12:10,790
the human imagination.

151
00:12:11,030 --> 00:12:11,910
Song Yang.

152
00:12:12,110 --> 00:12:13,440
I want to understand humans better.

153
00:12:13,630 --> 00:12:14,860
And understand you better.

154
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,350
Back to the point.

155
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:23,910
I've noticed that
these three murder cases

156
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,200
all share

157
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,710
a striking similarity.

158
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:28,790
- The condition of the bodies...
- Are those the three murder cases

159
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:30,440
where three people were brutally killed

160
00:12:30,710 --> 00:12:32,030
one after another on the same night,

161
00:12:32,230 --> 00:12:33,400
their eyes gouged out,

162
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:34,440
and the killer has never been found?

163
00:12:34,590 --> 00:12:35,000
Exactly.

164
00:12:35,150 --> 00:12:36,590
And the condition of the bodies
was very...

165
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,080
Wait.

166
00:12:38,790 --> 00:12:39,590
How did you know?

167
00:12:40,790 --> 00:12:42,590
I read about them in a novel.

168
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:44,590
The author is Zhang Mingxuan.

169
00:12:44,710 --> 00:12:46,000
His novel The Survivor

170
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,030
made him famous overnight.

171
00:12:56,550 --> 00:12:58,520
Zhang Mingxuan?

172
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:00,500
(Zhang Mingxuan's profile)

173
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:18,260
♪I'm the one who's broken♪

174
00:13:19,090 --> 00:13:23,960
♪Calm, ordinary, and reckless♪

175
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,870
♪That's me, too♪

176
00:13:28,410 --> 00:13:31,930
♪Carefully sketching
and shaping every detail♪

177
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:36,230
♪Laughter and tears make life feel real♪

178
00:13:36,850 --> 00:13:40,640
♪Don't fear that it's not worth it.
Just be brave♪

179
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:43,490
♪And learn from your mistakes♪

180
00:13:45,430 --> 00:13:48,090
♪If the human heart
is impossible to fathom♪

181
00:13:48,090 --> 00:13:50,220
♪Could selling my soul and body♪

182
00:13:50,220 --> 00:13:53,390
♪Bring me something more?♪

183
00:13:54,090 --> 00:14:00,820
♪Stroke by stroke,
I draw the perfect outline♪

184
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:05,050
♪Sadness is blue♪

185
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:09,270
♪How would you paint me?♪

186
00:14:10,270 --> 00:14:14,000
♪Layering, crossing, blending endlessly♪

187
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:16,260
♪Painting without restraint♪

188
00:14:16,450 --> 00:14:19,040
♪Covering the person I used to be♪

189
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:23,230
♪If I could start over♪

190
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:27,300
♪I'd show more feeling
in every look and gesture♪

191
00:14:27,410 --> 00:14:30,050
♪Give me back my smile♪

192
00:14:30,650 --> 00:14:33,130
♪Find joy even in hardship♪

193
00:14:33,630 --> 00:14:38,870
♪Don't let the next version of me
be left with nothing♪

